Window glass follows the renderer's modifier.

A view that draws windows somewhere else and smaller than they are (the
stackzoom plugin's zoomed-out view of the workspaces) does it through
SRenderModifData, inside the monitor's own frame. Any render with a modifier
counted as foreign and got no glass at all, and the glass knew only the
window's real box.

- RenderGuards::isForeignTarget(): the capture and other-framebuffer part of
  isForeignRender(). renderPass() asks that one, so a modifier alone no longer
  turns the glass off; everything else keeps the full check.
- renderPass() puts the box through ctx.m_data.renderModif. The corner radius
  stays as it is: Hyprland draws the border and clips the surface with the
  full radius under a modifier too, and a pane with a scaled one showed its
  corners outside the border's curve.
- Under a modifier the pane's alpha leaves out the workspace's: a row that is
  not the shown workspace has alpha 0 there, and its terminals lost their
  glass body until the row was selected.
- The cached sample is taken again whenever the box it is drawn at changes
  under a modifier: what lies behind the pane changes with it, and nothing the
  cache watches knows.
- Frost coverage is still measured where the windows are.

